      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-224345",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following statement:\n\n> Let $x\u223cy$ if and only if $x + y$ is an even number for $x, y \u2208 Z$. Then, $\u223c$ is a symmetric relation on $Z$.\n\nA proof of this statement is given below.\n\n> $L1$: Let $x, y \u2208 Z$ and $x\u223cy$.\n> $L2$: Then, $x + y$ is an even number.\n> $L3$: So, $y + x = x + y$ is an even number.\n> $L4$: Thus, $y\u223cx$.\n> $L5$: Therefore, $\u223c$ is symmetric on $Z$.\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nLine $L2$ follows from line $L1$ by the definition of {{field-1}}.\n\nLine $L5$ follows from $L1$ and $L4$ by the {{field-2}} of {{field-3}}.\n\nTo prove that $\u223c$ is an equivalence relation, we also need to demonstrate that $\u223c$ is {{field-4}} and {{field-5}}."
